\details{
Discard mortality defines the proportion of discarded catch that dies.
Fish that are selected but not retained (as defined by \code{\link[=Retention]{Retention()}}) are
treated as discards; \code{DiscardMortality} determines how many of those fish
die as a result of the capture-and-release process.

Unlike \code{\link[=Selectivity]{Selectivity()}} and \code{\link[=Retention]{Retention()}}, discard mortality does not
support model-based population via \code{Pars} and \code{Model}. Values must be
supplied directly as \code{MeanAtAge} or \code{MeanAtLength} arrays. If neither is
supplied, \code{\link[=PopulateDiscardMortality]{PopulateDiscardMortality()}} defaults to 0 (all discards survive)
for all age and length classes.
\subsection{Array Format}{

\code{MeanAtAge} may be a scalar, a vector of length \code{nAge}, or a full
\verb{Sim x Age x Year} array. Scalars and vectors are wrapped internally to
arrays with a single simulation and year, then extended to cover all
simulations and years during population. If \code{MeanAtLength} is supplied, it
takes precedence and \code{MeanAtAge} is derived from it using the age-length
key.
}

\subsection{Attaching to a Fleet}{

A \link[=discardmortality-class]{discardmortality} object can be attached to a \code{\link[=Fleet]{Fleet()}} with
\code{DiscardMortality(Fleet) <- MyDiscardMortality} and retrieved with
\code{DiscardMortality(Fleet)}.

Individual slots may be accessed or modified using \code{\link[=MeanAtAge]{MeanAtAge()}},
\code{\link[=MeanAtLength]{MeanAtLength()}}, and \code{\link[=Classes]{Classes()}}.
}
}
\section{Pass-Through Access}{

When \code{MeanAtAge} is an object that contains \code{DiscardMortality} objects,
\code{DiscardMortality()} returns them instead of constructing a new object:
\itemize{
\item a \link[=fleet-class]{fleet} object: its \code{DiscardMortality} slot.
\item an \link[=om-class]{om}, \link[=hist-class]{hist}, or \link[=mse-class]{mse} object: a list by stock of
lists by fleet, with the \code{DiscardMortality} slot of each fleet. A list of
\link[=fleet-class]{fleet} objects, or a list of them by stock, returns a list with
the same structure.
\item a \link[=data-class]{data} or \link[=obs-class]{obs} object, or an \link[=exploitationdata-class]{exploitationdata} or
\link[=exploitationobs-class]{exploitationobs} object or a list of them: the \code{DiscardMortality} slot
of the exploitation information.
\item an \link[=advice-class]{advice} object: the discard mortality set by an MP. The slot of these objects can also be replaced.
}

\code{DiscardMortality(x) <- value} replaces the slot of a \link[=fleet-class]{fleet} or
\link[=om-class]{om} object, a \link[=data-class]{data} or \link[=obs-class]{obs} object, an
\link[=exploitationdata-class]{exploitationdata} or \link[=exploitationobs-class]{exploitationobs} object, or of
each object in a list of them. For an \link[=om-class]{om} object, \code{value} is a
single object when the OM has one stock and one fleet, a list named by
fleet (see \code{\link[=FleetNames]{FleetNames()}}) when it has one stock and several fleets, and a
list named by stock (see \code{\link[=StockNames]{StockNames()}}) of lists named by fleet when it
has several stocks. The slot cannot be replaced in a \link[=hist-class]{hist} or
\link[=mse-class]{mse} object, because it was used to simulate the historical
dynamics.
}

\examples{
## ---- Default: zero discard mortality ----
# An empty DiscardMortality object causes PopulateDiscardMortality() to set
# discard mortality to 0 for all age and length classes (all discards survive).
# This is the default when no DiscardMortality object is supplied to Fleet().
dm_empty <- DiscardMortality()
dm_empty

## ---- Constant discard mortality (scalar) ----
# A scalar is applied to all age classes across all simulations and years.
# Here 30\% of discarded fish die regardless of age.
dm_scalar <- DiscardMortality(MeanAtAge = 0.3)

## ---- Age-varying discard mortality (vector) ----
# A vector of length nAge specifies mortality per age class.
# Younger fish (smaller, more vulnerable) may have higher discard mortality.
ages    <- 0:20
dm_vals <- pmax(1 - ages / 10, 0)   # declines from 1 at age 0 to 0 at age 10

dm_vec <- DiscardMortality(MeanAtAge = dm_vals)

## ---- Full array (Sim x Age x Year) ----
# A full array allows discard mortality to vary across simulations and years.
dm_array <- array(
  0.2,
  dim      = c(1, length(ages), 1),
  dimnames = list(Sim = 1, Age = ages, Year = 2000)
)

dm_full <- DiscardMortality(MeanAtAge = dm_array)
MeanAtAge(dm_full)

## ---- Specifying discard mortality at length ----
# MeanAtLength takes precedence over MeanAtAge when both are supplied.
# MeanAtAge is derived from MeanAtLength via the age-length key during
# PopulateDiscardMortality().
lengths  <- seq(10, 100, by = 5)
dm_at_l  <- pmax(1 - lengths / 60, 0)   # mortality declines with length

dm_length_array <- array(
  dm_at_l,
  dim      = c(1, length(lengths), 1),
  dimnames = list(Sim = 1, Length = lengths, Year = 2000)
)

dm_len <- DiscardMortality(
  MeanAtLength = dm_length_array,
  Classes      = lengths
)
MeanAtLength(dm_len)

## ---- Attaching to a Fleet object ----
f <- Fleet(Name = "Trawl")
DiscardMortality(f) <- DiscardMortality(MeanAtAge = 0.2)
DiscardMortality(f)
MeanAtAge(DiscardMortality(f))

## ---- Extracting DiscardMortality from a Fleet ----
# Passing a fleet object as the first argument returns its DiscardMortality slot.
dm <- DiscardMortality(f)
dm
}
